      "writtenOn": "2020-09-21T16:33:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "trusty-core only builds for ARM and ARM64 for at least two reasons.  The main one is that it requires an implementation of trusty_smc8() which is written in assembly language.\n\nhttps://android-review.googlesource.com/c/kernel/common/+/1430106 adds the missing dependency on ARM||ARM64 to trusty-core.\n\nhttps://android-review.googlesource.com/c/kernel/common/+/1432995 removes CONFIG_TRUSTY_SMC_ARM and CONFIG_TRUSTY_SMC_ARM64 because we should just be using CONFIG_ARM and CONFIG_ARM64 instead.",
